From: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
Subject: [PATCH] ASoC: qcom: q6apm: reuse configured pull graph on prepare

The protected SP11 pull endpoint is configured once for the lifetime of its
graph.  ALSA may call prepare more than once on the same open stream,
including after STOP.  The existing generic path stops the graph and
resends the shared-memory endpoint configuration on every prepare.

The DSP rejects that second pull-ring transaction with AR_EALREADY.
Keep the persistent pull graph configured and running, and only re-arm
the host stream state on subsequent prepares.  This is pull-mode-only;
the endpoint's PCM constraints fix its format at 48 kHz, stereo, 16-bit,
with a 3,840-byte ring and two 1,920-byte periods.

Signed-off-by: SP11 audio reconstruction <sp11-audio@localhost>
---
 sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c | 13 +++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 13 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
--- a/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
+++ b/sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6/q6apm-dai.c
@@ -252,6 +252,19 @@ static int q6apm_dai_prepare(struct snd_soc_component *component,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The SP11 pull endpoint is configured once for the lifetime of its
+	 * graph.  ALSA may call prepare again on the same open stream, including
+	 * after STOP.  Re-sending the pull-ring parameter is rejected by the DSP
+	 * with AR_EALREADY, while the fixed 48 kHz stereo format cannot change.
+	 * Keep the persistent graph running and only re-arm the host-side state.
+	 */
+	if (prtd->graph->pull_mode && prtd->state != Q6APM_STREAM_IDLE) {
+		prtd->state = Q6APM_STREAM_RUNNING;
+		dev_info(dev, "SP11 stage duplicate prepare reused pull graph\n");
+		return 0;
+	}
+
 	cfg.direction = substream->stream;
 	cfg.sample_rate = runtime->rate;
 	cfg.num_channels = runtime->channels;
-- 
